Claim: card thread · `domain:services` seat 1 (seat post #6021, project run by the Sales account) · p2 · series card, cut 13 of the `security-plugin.ts` split: the `start()` row, part 3 — what `start()` registers after the authorization middleware (R4) moves out · 2026-10-24T03:32Z
Not Tier H. `node scripts/pm/check-governed-merges.mjs --test` on the trial file list (`security-plugin.ts` and the new module): 0 of 2 paths hit the register, NOT governed. Size about 1,000 changed lines (+551 / −448), under the 3,000-line line. So the landing is the ordinary queue landing after the seat's ACCEPT. I re-run the predicate on the final list with `--pr` once the PR exists.
Ruling-ref: 6353073966 (item 2 for the anchor reading); the series' `.d.ts` bar stays ruling 6348891160 item 1
Session: `session_017BoLT8Gaa8t9a7AWVH8qZa`
Account: `os-sales` (the seat's linked user; the card's assignee)
Branch: `claude/project-thread-3fzya4`, the harness-pinned branch for this session, restarted from `origin/main` at `e073455929`, which contains cut 12's merge (`df893f6d76`). It names no issue, so this claim is the identity record.
Worktree: `objectstack-issue-25223`
Domain: `domain:services` (the seat post's name; #25247 aliases it to `domain:server`)
Seat: `domain:services#1` (seat post #6021)

Why now: the seat's cut 12 landing note (6379109594) asks for R4 as cut 13 on the merged file, with `claimTargetAdminUserId` as a get/set host pair in the #25508 form. The seat's plan answer (10-23 19:20Z) already ruled that pair is not a new shape: #25224 cut 10 (PR #25508, `7d3c0139fb`) hosts `routeOwnership` the same way in `auth-manager-request-routing.ts`.

**R4 is the last movable row of `start()`, so this cut's report doubles as the series' final report.** After it, `start()` holds R1 (the setup, which writes 11 members and stays) and the three stub blocks of cuts 11, 12 and 13. `init()` stays, because ADR-0126:406 `#nav_permission_sets` resolves only on a literal there. The report will give `security-plugin.ts`'s line count at the start of the series and at the end, every body that stays with its reason, and every cut PR.

File surface, cut 13 (stop on a breach and explain it in the report). One seam, one new module.
- `packages/plugins/plugin-security/src/security-plugin.ts`, at `e073455929` (6,164 lines; `start()` is `:1744`-`:2619`, 48 statements):
  - To `security-plugin-start-hooks.ts` (host `StartHooksHost`), a RUN of statements: `start()`'s last 16 (33 to 48), `:2192`-`:2612` (421 lines, counted from the first statement's leading comment). In order, that run registers:
    - the `sys_user_position` catalog refusal middleware and the grant-holder membership refusal;
    - the permission-set name hooks, followed by the ADR-0131 D3 note;
    - the bootstrap once-guards and `runBootstrap`, with its `kernel:ready` registration;
    - the boot reports on `kernel:bootstrapped`;
    - the middleware that replays the bootstrap after a qualifying write;
    - the `sys_member` middleware that reconciles `organization_admin` grants;
    - `runOrgAdminBackfill`, with its `kernel:ready` registration.
  - It becomes `export function registerStartHooks(this: Pick<StartHooksHost, …>, ctx: PluginContext, ql: IObjectQLEngine): void`. Its body is the run, re-indented one level and otherwise unedited, with every comment above and between its statements.
    - Why the parameters: the run closes over two of `start()`'s locals, `ctx` and `ql`, and nothing else.
    - Measured on the AST: it has no `arguments`, `super` or bare `this`, no `this` inside a non-arrow function, and no `return`, `await`, `break` or `continue` at its top level.
    - The run's own eight locals (`bootstrapRanOnce`, `readSeedSettlement`, `everyoneMutationWired`, `catalogEchoWired`, `catalogEchoBooted`, `managedDeniesApplied`, `runBootstrap`, `runOrgAdminBackfill`) move with it. Nothing after the run reads them, because the run ends `start()`.
  - The stub is one block at the same position, now the last statement of `start()`. It holds the read and write locals, one host literal and `registerStartHooks.call(host, ctx, ql);`. The registrations stay synchronous and in the same order, right after the middleware's log line. The comment that closes `start()` (the per-organization seed DATA replay note) stays after the stub.
  - The host is #23050's shape B, as cuts 11 and 12 applied it to `start()`:
    - 3 methods as late-bound closures: `declareEveryone`, `deploymentAcceptance`, `deploymentOrgScopingEntitlement`;
    - `bootstrapPermissionSets`, declared `readonly`, by value. It is the same array, whose sets the managed-object denies extend in place;
    - `metadata` and `tenancyPosture`, which are not `readonly`, as getters, so each is read when the hooks run;
    - `claimTargetAdminUserId` as a **get/set pair**. It is the one member the run WRITES: `runBootstrap` records the platform admin it found or promoted (`:2281`). The pair takes #25508's form, so the write lands on the plugin, where cut 11's seed claim reads it through its own getter. Its host field is the one that is not `readonly`.
    - No receiver changes: every method call goes through the host's closure to the plugin's method, and each getter returns the plugin's own object.
  - No module-level declaration moves, because the run reads none.
  - Import names only the run reads leave `security-plugin.ts`, 26 in all. The module imports each from the specifier `security-plugin.ts` imports it from, and keeps its type-only-ness:
    - from `./position-catalog-refusal.js`: `POSITION_ASSIGNMENT_OBJECT`, `createPositionCatalogRefusal`;
    - from `./grant-holder-membership-refusal.js`: `registerGrantHolderMembershipRefusal`;
    - from `./grant-permission-set-name.js`: `registerGrantPermissionSetNameHooks`;
    - from `./catalog-reference-report.js`: `reportCatalogReferences`;
    - from `./access-upgrade-report.js`: `reportAccessUpgrade` and the type `AccessUpgradeNotifier`;
    - from `./upgrade-impact-report.js`: `reportUpgradeImpact`, `SETTINGS_SERVICE` and the type `SettingsManifestReader`;
    - from `./managed-object-write-denies.js`: `applyManagedWriteDenies`;
    - from `./packaged-permission-set-overlay-detection.js`: `reportPackagedPermissionSetOverlays`;
    - from `./object-posture-gate.js`: `registerObjectPostureGate`;
    - from `./packaged-permission-set-lock-gate.js`: `registerPackagedPermissionSetLockGate`;
    - from `./security-catalog-echo.js`: `registerSecurityCatalogEcho`, `echoStoredSecurityCatalogOverlays`;
    - from `./suggested-audience-bindings.js`: `reconcileAudienceBindingSuggestions`;
    - from `./cleanup-package-permissions.js`: `cleanupPackagePermissions`;
    - from `./declared-capability-context.js`: `readDeclared`;
    - from `./security-plugin-seed-claim.js`: `readSeedSettlementSnapshot`;
    - from `./bootstrap-platform-admin.js`: `bootstrapPlatformAdmin`, `shouldReplayBootstrapFor`;
    - from `./auto-org-admin-grant.js`: `backfillOrgAdminGrants`, `extractMemberPairs`, `reconcileOrgAdminGrant`;
    - from `@objectstack/spec/contracts`: the type `SeedSettlementSnapshot`.
  - Six names stay in `security-plugin.ts` because staying code reads them too, and the module imports them from the same specifiers: `PluginContext`, `createSecurityCatalogReader`, `postureEnforcesWall`, `SHARING_RULES_SERVICE`, `DeclaredSharingRuleReader`, `IObjectQLEngine`. The module imports the class type-only, and `security-plugin.ts` gains no `export`.
  - One import becomes type-only, and one comment line set is rewritten. Both are disclosed:
    - `readSeededRecordIds` (cut 11's seed-claim module) is read by the run alone, but `claimSeedOwnershipOnSettle`'s staying docblock links to it (`{@link readSeededRecordIds}`, `:1728`). It stays in that import, type-only, so the link still resolves. Cuts 6 (`principalLessDenial`) and 12 (`WriteImageCheckSeam`) are the precedent.
    - The 4-line cut 11 comment above that import says this file imports "the two `seed-settlement` readers it shares with the promotion-time pass in `start()`". That pass moves, so the comment becomes 6 lines that say where the readers are imported now and why `readSeededRecordIds` stays type-only. No other comment in `security-plugin.ts` changes.
- Readers that key on the moved lines: none found. Each was measured on the trial, not recalled:
  - R4 holds no `isSystem` read and no tenant-audit site. `isystem-census` gives 149 sites and `tenant-audit-census` 238 at both ends, with 0 differences and 0 sites in the new module. `check-system-context-census` output is byte-identical at both ends, so `system-context.mdx` and the ledger are untouched.
  - R4 makes no `canReadObject` call (the core row-serving pin) and resolves no delegator (the #25107 pin).
  - The platform checklist's `security-plugin.ts#declareEveryone` resolves on the method, which stays.
  - No test that reads `security-plugin.ts` by path names R4's content.
  - The suite and every derived gate run at both ends before the hand-off.
- `scripts/adr-anchors/`: no new entry, and the `security-plugin.ts` entry is unchanged. Disclosed:
  - That entry's ADR-0138 D1 paragraph says the seed-ownership claim "this file runs on every `app:seeded` (`claimSeedOwnershipOnSettle`) and at the first promotion" re-owns a NULL-owner row only when the seed reported landing on it (`readSeededRecordIds`).
  - The first-promotion arm, `runBootstrap`'s `seededRecordIds: readSeededRecordIds(ctx)`, moves into the new module. The run cites no ADR-0138, so an entry for the new module would need a citation the moved code does not carry, and this cut plants none. Cut 12's ADR-0123 D2 disclosure is the precedent.
  - The `security-plugin.ts` entry still holds. The claim method and the `readSeededRecordIds` import stay in the file, and `start()` still registers the first-promotion pass through the stub. But cut 11's claim (6373426297) gave three reasons why that entry stays true: the method, the promotion-time pass and the import. The second of those now lives in the module.
  - The seed-claim module's own entry is unaffected. The seat may want this as a follow-up.
- Decision letters. `check:adr-anchors` counts them only on the anchored surface (84 files at both ends).
  - On the merge-base `e073455929`: **1888**. With the cut in place: **1877**.
  - All −11 are R4's letters leaving `security-plugin.ts`, which holds 185 such citations at base and 174 with the cut: ADR-0090 D5 ×3, ADR-0131 D3 ×3, and ×1 each ADR-0057 D4, ADR-0086 D1, ADR-0090 D11, ADR-0131 D10 and ADR-0131 D4.
  - Five letters leave `security-plugin.ts` entirely: ADR-0057 D4, ADR-0086 D1, ADR-0090 D11, ADR-0131 D10 and ADR-0131 D4.
  - No letter is planted and none is invented. Repo-wide citations stay at 52,315, because the module header cites no ADR.
- Every other gate, baseline, docs anchor and test that reads a moved line by path moves in the same PR and stays green. ⛔ No gate is loosened, and none goes silently empty.
- `.d.ts`: ruling 6348891160 item 1, with the same four-hash block, normaliser, raw line count and positive control as cuts 1 to 12.
  - Measured on full builds at both ends: `dist/index.d.ts` and `index.d.mts` are byte-identical to base (`7e6a99f7…`, 14,722 lines; normalised `e22a714d…`).
  - The positive control (`private` removed from `epoch`, real rebuild) gives `96fda037…`. The restored rebuild gives `7e6a99f7…` again.
- Bundle, disclosed. Both built bundles load (`import()` and `require`) with the same 66 exports (key-list hash `df56a808` at both ends).
  - Thirteen module chunks are emitted later in `index.mjs`, because `security-plugin.ts` no longer imports them first. Ten are modules whose import leaves `security-plugin.ts` whole: `position-catalog-refusal`, `grant-holder-membership-refusal`, `catalog-reference-report`, `upgrade-impact-report`, `managed-object-write-denies`, `packaged-permission-set-overlay-detection`, `object-posture-gate`, `packaged-permission-set-lock-gate`, `security-catalog-echo` and `cleanup-package-permissions`. The other three are modules those ten import: `federated-phantom-anchors`, `packaged-permission-set-lock` and `objects/sys-user-position.object`.
  - None imports `security-plugin.ts`.
  - Their top level only declares: constants, functions, classes, a `Set`, a `WeakMap`, and one `ObjectSchema.create(…)` (a validating constructor from `@objectstack/spec`, outside the bundle; it registers nothing).
- No changeset (`skip-changeset`).
- ⛔ Not touched: R1, the stubs of cuts 11 and 12, `init()`, every other class member, and any behaviour.

Proof, on the trial (scratch `proof.cjs`, every check against the base file):
- the function body is the run's text, less two spaces, from the first comment line to the last statement's end. That is 16 statements, 421 lines and 1,610 tokens;
- `start()` is byte-identical to base outside the run, which is now an 18-line stub block;
- the host literal, the host interface and the function's `this` `Pick` are the same 7 members, each in the form its own declaration calls for, with the written member as the get/set pair;
- the other 125 class members and the constructor are byte-identical;
- 84 top-level statements are byte-identical, and only imports differ: 27 names dropped (26 plus the value import of `readSeededRecordIds`) and 3 added (`registerStartHooks`, type `StartHooksHost`, type `readSeededRecordIds`);
- the module's top level is its imports, `StartHooksHost` and `registerStartHooks`, and nothing else.
14 negative controls, each a one-token mutation, are each caught by the check named for them. They include a token in the run, a comment between its statements, the setter dropped, the written field made `readonly`, a read-only field made writable, the setter writing a different value, and `readSeededRecordIds` kept as a value import.

Anchor and reader reading before the cut (ruling item 2), on `e073455929`, with the cut in place:
- ADR anchors into `security-plugin.ts` or the new module, mapped with `extractAnchors` and `symbolSegmentResolution` from `scripts/symbol-anchors.mjs`: 26 citing lines over 17 symbols. None changes path or class, and none resolves inside R4. ADR-0126:406 `#nav_permission_sets` stays a `literal` in `init`.
- `node scripts/check-adr-symbol-anchors.mjs` exits 0 at both ends (2,384 anchors over 142 records).

Serial check: none of the 11 open PRs touches `security-plugin.ts` or any `security-plugin-*.ts` module (read at 03:20Z). I re-list them right before `pr_create`.

